\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces The \texttt  {spi\_display} shifter. A TXDATA write loads the byte and pulls SCK low with the MSB already on SDA; each bit then spends half a $\div 6$ period low (data driven) and half high (panel samples, mode 3); after the eighth bit SCK parks high, which \emph  {is} the mode 3 idle, so byte boundaries need no extra states.}}{24}{figure.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:disp-fsm}{{16}{24}{The \texttt {spi\_display} shifter. A TXDATA write loads the byte and pulls SCK low with the MSB already on SDA; each bit then spends half a $\div 6$ period low (data driven) and half high (panel samples, mode 3); after the eighth bit SCK parks high, which \emph {is} the mode 3 idle, so byte boundaries need no extra states}{figure.caption.29}{}}
